      "description": "The Lean templates this harness's tooling fills: today `formal-edges.lean.tmpl`, which pipeline/formal-edges.ts writes into a folio's own `.lake/` and elaborates there. Declared with graph typology `lean`, the kind this instance owns for Lean sources (typologies/lean.json), on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-10: \"lean/ is a declared directory in folio-asst-sci (it should be) and lean Processes and Tools are around that.\" The Tools (`lean-html-docs`, `lean-render-publish`), the process (`lean-docs-publish`) and the skill (`lean-html-docs`) are what a FOLIO's `lean` directory gets: its doc-gen4 render, published under the folio's site in the harness rail. `.tmpl`, never `.lean`: the platform tracks no Lean content, and lean-decl-starts-are-shared.test.ts holds it to that. Declared WITH its files, per bean dh4f.",
